Chrome's platform sections in the User-Agent, OpenHarmony and ArkWeb at the end.

A phone sends Chrome's reduced Android User-Agent. Append the OpenHarmony
version as a product token, "... Mobile Safari/537.36 OpenHarmony/7.0",
so that sites looking for HarmonyOS find it while the platform section
stays exactly Chrome's: with "OpenHarmony 7.0" inside it, in front of the
Android token or after it, the phone failed Cloudflare Turnstile. The
version is the system's (OH_GetOSFullName), major.minor; the client hints
stay Android.

Tablets, 2in1s and unfolded foldables did the same with ArkWeb's own
shape, "(Tablet; OpenHarmony 7.0) ... ArkWeb/7.0.0.105", and failed
Turnstile with 600010 whenever client hints went with it, as ArkWeb itself
does. They now send Chrome's Linux section naming the real CPU, with
OpenHarmony as a product at the end and no ArkWeb token,
"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux aarch64) ... Safari/537.36 OpenHarmony/7.0",
with the HarmonyOS client hints unchanged; measured on a tablet, the X11
section passed with UA-CH platform Linux or HarmonyOS, the old shape never. navigator.platform says
"Linux aarch64" to match. The Chrome Web Store user agent no longer adds
X11 where the section already has it.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-phone-ua-openharmony.patch

